module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_discarded_write_result_reads_a_lost_settlement_as_persisted

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { NoRungStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

// Consumer: directory-derived recurring_failure_mode.roster, projected by
// gunbc.design_ledgers.expected_design_failure_modes_md through docs_projection_gate.
data a_discarded_write_result_reads_a_lost_settlement_as_persisted: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_discarded_write_result_reads_a_lost_settlement_as_persisted" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: NoRungStated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: belt_commit_outcome_persist ignored the Filesystem.Write result, so the outcome record, the durable capture-settled fact worktree release reads, could be absent while the step reported persisted. HARM: a lost settlement write is indistinguishable from a settled capture; downstream treats the capture as settled or never retries it (silent wrongness, DESIGN section 5). Found by PR 14235 slice 3 at mitigatable.  DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the effect result was dropped at the call, so nothing in the types or a happy-path run differs; only a failing write shows it. Red-on-main receipt: PR 14235 body, belt_commit_outcome_persist_wet_witness passed on the branch and failed on main (behavioural RED, same cell).",

    "RUNG NOW: mitigatable. The write is checked and a failure returns CommitFailed, which no caller treats as settled. Executed evidence: test.claim.roadmap.belt_commit_outcome_persist_wet_witness. The class (an effect result discarded) is still writable elsewhere. CEILING: structurally guaranteed, since a dropped effect result is decidable from the Node tree. NEXT TRIGGER: can climb now but unbuilt, a lens or compiler refusal on any Filesystem.Write result not consumed; the site census is not a prerequisite. The census prerequisite is retired by the 2026-10-30 process ruling (`gunbc.design_ruling bad_process_is_worse_than_no_process`); this does not establish corpus-wide coverage, and changes use scoped review and focused tests.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.roadmap.belt_commit_outcome_persist_wet_witness", decl_name: "live_tree_disposition", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_commit_outcome_persist", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
